            <ArticleTitle>Severe hypophosphataemia induced by glucose-insulin-potassium therapy. A case report and proposal for altered protocol.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>327-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case is described where severe hypophosphataemia was induced by a widely used protocol for glucose-insulin-potassium (GIK) infusion. Hypophosphataemia was found to be a universal sequel to the use of this infusion. A new regimen for administering this agent was designed, and shown to lack the potentially serious side effect of phosphate depletion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
